001: spec:
002:   grid: 30x30 fixed
003:   background: 0
004:   foreground: single color (always 3 [observed])
005:   rooms:
006:     count: 6-8 non-overlapping hollow rectangular frames
007:     dimensions: 3-11 rows x 3-11 cols; mix of small (3-4) and medium/large (5-12)
008:     structure: exactly 1-cell-thick border, interior is background
009:   candidate_edges:
010:     definition: |
011:       pair of rooms separated horizontally or vertically with:
012:       (a) overlapping interiors in the perpendicular axis (>=1 cell),
013:       (b) the rectangular gap region between them is all background
014:     count: n_rooms-1 to n_rooms (nearly a tree; at most 1 extra edge)
015:     gap_distance: 1-7 cells between facing walls
016:     overlap: 1-7 cells of shared interior range
017:   spanning_tree:
018:     algorithm: Kruskal MST by gap distance; all same-gap edges connecting new components added together
019:     chosen_edges: exactly n_rooms - 1 (forms a spanning tree)
020:   output_transform:
021:     for each chosen edge, draw a corridor connecting two rooms:
022:       horizontal - paint top/bottom rows of overlap across gap; erase facing wall cells between those rows
023:       vertical - paint left/right cols of overlap across gap; erase facing wall cells between those cols
024:     result is one 4-connected component
025: 
026: generation_strategy:
027:   approach: output-first (build connected corridor network, then remove corridors to get input)
028:   steps:
029:     1. Choose n_rooms in [6,8]. Build a random spanning tree on n_rooms nodes.
030:     2. For each tree edge, assign direction (h or v) and gap distance (1-7).
031:     3. Place rooms on 30x30 grid using tree structure. For each room pick size 3-11 x 3-11.
032:        Place rooms so each tree edge has the assigned gap and >=1 interior overlap.
033:        Use constraint propagation or sequential placement along BFS order from root.
034:     4. Verify all rooms fit in grid, don't overlap, and gap regions are clear background.
035:        Optionally add 0-1 extra candidate edges (redundant paths rejected by MST).
036:     5. Draw all hollow frames. This is the INPUT.
037:     6. Run solver (_spanning_edges + _apply_edge) to produce OUTPUT.
038:     Retry placement if constraints fail; tree-guided placement keeps rejection low.
